  "name": "Yeve (Ewe thunder-cult ritual music)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Ritual music of Yeve, the Ewe vodu society devoted to the thunder deity Xebieso (So), centred in Anlo and other Ewe areas of Ghana and Togo. Its ceremonies run through a sequence of distinct dance-drumming pieces, among them sovu, sogba and husago, sung by initiates over drums, iron bells and rattles; the Ewe drum, bell and rattle cards stand in for the society's own set.",
